From 7a25bcf9cde8879b21cb50e26decb1dbf049a4b3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ahmad Fatoum <ahmad@a3f.at>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 22:44:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] umpf: add range-diff command

After rebasing an umpf onto a new base, a plain git diff between the old
and the new utag also contains all upstream changes. git range-diff shows
how the patch stack itself changed, but needs the base and the flat tip
of both umpfs, which umpf already knows.

Add "umpf range-diff <old> [<new>]", which takes utags or qualified
useries files (e.g. from format-patch), and passes options after '--'
on to git range-diff.

The release commits of both umpfs only change the version, but after a
rebase, their context often differs as well, e.g. SUBLEVEL. With the
default creation factor of 60, git range-diff shows such a small commit
as dropped and added instead of changed, so use 100.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
